Q: Join two tables in MySQL with random rows from the second A: <p>You want each record from table1 with exactly 5 random records from table2 ?</p>
<p>Create a full join with 5 dynamic columns, each consisting of a random <code>id</code> from <code>table2</code> (taking unique values in account):</p>
<pre class="lang-sql prettyprint-override"><code>SELECT `table1`.`id` AS `t1_id`,
             @r1 AS `rand1`,
             @r2 AS `rand2`,
             @r3 AS `rand3`,
             @r4 AS `rand4`,
             @r5 AS `rand5`
      FROM
          `table1`
      WHERE `table1`.`id` = IF(
              ((@r1 := (SELECT `id` FROM `table2` ORDER BY RAND() LIMIT 1)) OR TRUE) AND
              ((@r2 := (SELECT `id` FROM `table2` WHERE `id` NOT IN (@r1) ORDER BY RAND() LIMIT 1)) OR TRUE) AND
              ((@r3 := (SELECT `id` FROM `table2` WHERE `id` NOT IN (@r1, @r2)  ORDER BY RAND() LIMIT 1)) OR TRUE) AND
              ((@r4 := (SELECT `id` FROM `table2` WHERE `id` NOT IN (@r1, @r2, @r3)  ORDER BY RAND() LIMIT 1)) OR TRUE) AND
              ((@r5 := (SELECT `id` FROM `table2` WHERE `id` NOT IN (@r1, @r2, @r3, @r4)  ORDER BY RAND() LIMIT 1)) OR TRUE),
              `table1`.`id`,
              1
              )
</code></pre>
<p>The <code>IF()</code> statement is a nice but complex looking feature I regulary use, more on that here: <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/76959645/3090890">https://stackoverflow.com/a/76959645/3090890</a></p>
<p>Then you'll have each <code>table1</code> record with 5 random id's of <code>table2</code>, so you can join on them using that as subquery:</p>
<pre class="lang-sql prettyprint-override"><code>SET @r1=0;
SET @r2=0;
SET @r3=0;
SET @r4=0;
SET @r5=0;

SELECT
    `t1_id`,
    `table2`.`id` AS `t2_id`
FROM
    `table1`
JOIN
    (SELECT `table1`.`id` AS `t1_id`,
             @r1 AS `rand1`,
             @r2 AS `rand2`,
             @r3 AS `rand3`,
             @r4 AS `rand4`,
             @r5 AS `rand5`
      FROM
          `table1`
      WHERE `table1`.`id` = IF(
              ((@r1 := (SELECT `id` FROM `table2` ORDER BY RAND() LIMIT 1)) OR TRUE) AND
              ((@r2 := (SELECT `id` FROM `table2` WHERE `id` NOT IN (@r1) ORDER BY RAND() LIMIT 1)) OR TRUE) AND
              ((@r3 := (SELECT `id` FROM `table2` WHERE `id` NOT IN (@r1, @r2)  ORDER BY RAND() LIMIT 1)) OR TRUE) AND
              ((@r4 := (SELECT `id` FROM `table2` WHERE `id` NOT IN (@r1, @r2, @r3)  ORDER BY RAND() LIMIT 1)) OR TRUE) AND
              ((@r5 := (SELECT `id` FROM `table2` WHERE `id` NOT IN (@r1, @r2, @r3, @r4)  ORDER BY RAND() LIMIT 1)) OR TRUE),
              `table1`.`id`,
              1
              )
     ) AS `sub` ON (`sub`.`t1_id` = `table1`.`id`)
JOIN
    `table2` ON (`table2`.`id` IN (`sub`.`rand1`, `sub`.`rand2`, `sub`.`rand3`, `sub`.`rand4`, `sub`.`rand5`))
ORDER BY
    `t1_id`, `t2_id`;
</code></pre>
